From 24be0455118f813af56c862ce2f3170e9af85a52 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 20:42:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mix.json: the chase view 4.4 dB louder
 (air.closeView.masterDb 7.5): the Bremen chase-view film measured under its
 target

The game's first chase-view film (behind a Fw 190, patch one only) measured -16.4 LUFS against the
-12 LUFS the close view was set for (Brian's waist-gunner clip: -11.9; the ride he asked to be louder: -12.9).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01L4rhz35oCkUv94Xb2EwCjp
---
 unreal/TheaterCommand/Content/Data/Sound/mix.json | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/unreal/TheaterCommand/Content/Data/Sound/mix.json b/unreal/TheaterCommand/Content/Data/Sound/mix.json
index ce37efee..ea5b3cb9 100644
--- a/unreal/TheaterCommand/Content/Data/Sound/mix.json
+++ b/unreal/TheaterCommand/Content/Data/Sound/mix.json
@@ -1,7 +1,7 @@
 {
   "what": "The battle mix: how every approved battle sound is blended by unit, distance and how hot the fight is, so a battle plays like a war film. Numbers are the sound director's to tune; the 3D game reads them. Spec in plain words: battle-mix.md beside this file.",
   "version": 5,
-  "changes": "v5 (21 Nov, release 2; the 3D game's second air sound patch, sound/air-r2/): rounds striking a plane (air.roundsHit, silent until Brian marks round seven's hits Good); close flak in every view (air.closeView.closeFlak); big moments dip the rest in the air battle (big, air.bigDuck); dead engines thin the drones (air.engineLost); the battle's music driven by the air battle's own meter (music._air). Land (the ground battle sound thread): a new top-level `land` block, which touches no existing row. No number changed. v4's changes: mix-v4.json beside this file. After the review (21 Nov, 19:40Z), no number changed: air.roundsPassing.reach (new, 1000 m: rounds crack past beyond the guns' convergence); a fighter's fixed guns of one kind are one take (air.gunsByCalibre._wing); close flak is always heard (air.closeView.closeFlak._always); formation loops in air.loopsFamily, as written here; the master limiter's knee hard (buses.master._knee). Land block updated 21 Nov 19:25Z by the ground sound thread: land.mgClose.endFade 0.04 replaces tail, tailFade and farTail, and land.cracks.runFade 0.04 replaces runTail (the MG recordings fire on after a burst's last round, so the 0.3 s tail was about eight more rounds at full level). Land block updated 21 Nov 19:36Z by the ground sound thread: land.garand.reloadFromClips and reloadPieces (the reload heard from the clip recordings), and land.smgCue (the squad leader's Thompson burst, MP 38 takes standing in until a real Thompson is recorded). Land block updated 21 Nov 19:39Z by the ground sound thread: land.smgCue.leaderRoles (officer, leader), and the Garand reload and the leader's Thompson switch on by themselves at the first clip cue (notes only; the code default matches). The master limiter's detector (21 Nov 19:50Z): digital, 5 ms look-ahead (buses.master._detector); no number changed. 21 Nov 19:50Z: limits.worldTotal 64 (was 40; limits._worldTotal says why), and the ground sound thread's land block of 19:46Z: land.bodyCues.field_gun_breech null (no recording; the gun's case clangs anyway). Land block updated 21 Nov 20:12Z by the ground sound thread: land.bodyCues.medic_tend null (the medic's cue, silent until a real take passes) and land.armourStrikes (rounds on a tank's armour; its list is empty, so nothing changes until round eight's steel hits pass).",
+  "changes": "v5 (21 Nov, release 2; the 3D game's second air sound patch, sound/air-r2/): rounds striking a plane (air.roundsHit, silent until Brian marks round seven's hits Good); close flak in every view (air.closeView.closeFlak); big moments dip the rest in the air battle (big, air.bigDuck); dead engines thin the drones (air.engineLost); the battle's music driven by the air battle's own meter (music._air). Land (the ground battle sound thread): a new top-level `land` block, which touches no existing row. No number changed. v4's changes: mix-v4.json beside this file. After the review (21 Nov, 19:40Z), no number changed: air.roundsPassing.reach (new, 1000 m: rounds crack past beyond the guns' convergence); a fighter's fixed guns of one kind are one take (air.gunsByCalibre._wing); close flak is always heard (air.closeView.closeFlak._always); formation loops in air.loopsFamily, as written here; the master limiter's knee hard (buses.master._knee). Land block updated 21 Nov 19:25Z by the ground sound thread: land.mgClose.endFade 0.04 replaces tail, tailFade and farTail, and land.cracks.runFade 0.04 replaces runTail (the MG recordings fire on after a burst's last round, so the 0.3 s tail was about eight more rounds at full level). Land block updated 21 Nov 19:36Z by the ground sound thread: land.garand.reloadFromClips and reloadPieces (the reload heard from the clip recordings), and land.smgCue (the squad leader's Thompson burst, MP 38 takes standing in until a real Thompson is recorded). Land block updated 21 Nov 19:39Z by the ground sound thread: land.smgCue.leaderRoles (officer, leader), and the Garand reload and the leader's Thompson switch on by themselves at the first clip cue (notes only; the code default matches). The master limiter's detector (21 Nov 19:50Z): digital, 5 ms look-ahead (buses.master._detector); no number changed. 21 Nov 19:50Z: limits.worldTotal 64 (was 40; limits._worldTotal says why), and the ground sound thread's land block of 19:46Z: land.bodyCues.field_gun_breech null (no recording; the gun's case clangs anyway). Land block updated 21 Nov 20:12Z by the ground sound thread: land.bodyCues.medic_tend null (the medic's cue, silent until a real take passes) and land.armourStrikes (rounds on a tank's armour; its list is empty, so nothing changes until round eight's steel hits pass). 21 Nov 20:50Z: air.closeView.masterDb 7.5 (was 3.1): the game's chase view measured 4.4 dB under the -12 LUFS the close view was set for (air.closeView._masterDb says how).",
   "made": "2026-11-21",
   "files": "/mnt/project-files/sound/battle-pack/wav/",
   "units": "metres of the battlefield (the sims' x, y), seconds, decibels. 0 dB = the file as made.",
@@ -746,8 +746,8 @@
         },
         "_how": "one compressor on the world buses (bed, loops, close, big; not music), after their gains and the big moments' duck, before closeView.masterDb and the master limiter (buses.master.limiterCeilingDb, -1.5 dBFS). kneeDb is the knee's whole width (the renders used ffmpeg's acompressor with knee=2.82, a factor, which is 9 dB)."
       },
-      "masterDb": 3.1,
-      "_masterDb": "a fixed gain over the battle's master in the close view, in place of masterDbByCameraDistance. A game sets a gain; it does not measure a mix twice. Chosen so this raid's close view measures about -12 LUFS (it measures -11.7)",
+      "masterDb": 7.5,
+      "_masterDb": "a fixed gain over the battle's master in the close view, in place of masterDbByCameraDistance. A game sets a gain; it does not measure a mix twice. 7.5 from 21 Nov 20:50Z (was 3.1, chosen from the renders, where a B-17's close view measured -11.7 LUFS). The game's first chase-view film (Bremen, behind a Fw 190, patch one only) measured -16.4 LUFS before the builder's -1 dB, -19 LUFS between attacks, against -12.9 LUFS for the ride Brian asked to be louder and -11.9 for his waist-gunner clip: +4.4 dB puts it at about -12. It goes with part two, whose one-take-per-wing guns lower a Fw 190's own bursts about 6 dB, and needs the master limiter acting in what the film records (that film's peaks passed the ceiling 28 times, for up to 96 ms). With the bed's +6 dB the ridden plane's engine asks +13.5 dB, and Unreal holds any one sound at +12 dB at most.",
       "width": 1.0,
       "_width": "every sound panned at this share of its true angle. The close view's camera is outside the plane, so nothing smears where a sound is, as a fuselage would for an ear inside: the full angle. Measured left/right correlation: 0.99 at the inside sketch's 0.4 (v2), 0.96 at 0.6, 0.93 at 0.8, 0.89 at 1.0 (clip 2: 0.90)"
     },
